<Item XName="Constants" UserName="Constants" Type="Equation">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>Fsignal = tune(10);&#x0009;% Frequency of the CW signal in GHz&#x000D;&#x000A;Farray  = 10;       % Freq for the absolute spacing of the array elements, GHz&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;NumElements = tune(8);    % number of array elements Num * Num = Num^2&#x000D;&#x000A;SpeedOfLight = 299792458; % meter/sec&#x000D;&#x000A;HalfWavelength = 0.5*SpeedOfLight/(Farray * 1e9);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%These eqquations are used for the RX case, which is not applicable for TX&#x000D;&#x000A;% ArrayState = tune(2);    % 1=Rx, 2=Tx&#x000D;&#x000A;% RxPwrDensity_dBm = -50;&#x0009; % dBm&#x000D;&#x000A;% RxPwrIn_Watts = 10^( ( RxPwrDensity_dBm - 30 ) / 10 ) * (2*HalfWavelength)^2 / ( 4 * pi );&#x000D;&#x000A;% RxPwrIn_dBm = dbm( RxPwrIn_Watts);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;PhiCutAngle = tune(0);&#x000D;&#x000A;beamTheta = tune(20); %deg&#x000D;&#x000A;beamPhi = tune(0); %deg</Text>
